section: networking
title: Networking
about: |
  The zones, the subnets, the CIDRs, the routes, and the endpoints that a build needs. The section
  with the most rows and the least evidence: the lab runs go here first.
rules:
- id: ntp-servers
  title: The NTP servers of the cluster are addresses, and a cluster that needs them has some
  engines:
  - maas
  - edge
  - vsphere
  tier: static
  severity: warn
  status: source
  what: |
    The converter refuses an entry of `ntpServers` that is not an IPv4, IPv6, or DNS name. With
    no server, a vSphere cluster drifts: the docs recommend NTP servers. A multi-node edge cluster
    needs synchronized time; the cluster setting overwrites the per-host TUI and user-data
    setting, and with none each host keeps its own. MAAS gives its machines the time of the
    region controller, so an empty list is not a fault there. No check reaches the servers from
    the site; the reproduce line asks one from this machine.
  check:
    kind: static
    expr: |
      def is_addr: test("^([0-9]{1,3}\\.){3}[0-9]{1,3}$") or test("^[a-z0-9]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?(\\.[a-z0-9]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?)+$"; "i") or test("^[0-9a-f:]+$"; "i");
      .cloud as $cloud
      | ((.entity.spec.cloudConfig.ntpServers // []) | map(select(. != ""))) as $ntp
      | ([ .entity.spec.machinepoolconfig[] | (.cloudConfig.edgeHosts // []) | length ] | add // 0) as $hosts
      | [ ( $ntp[] | select(is_addr | not) | "ntpServers entry \(.) is not an address or a host name: the converter refuses the create" ),
          ( if ($ntp | length) == 0 then
              (if $cloud == "vsphere" then "no NTP server: the docs recommend NTP servers for a vSphere cluster, and without them the nodes drift"
               elif $cloud == "edge" and $hosts > 1 then "no NTP server on a multi-node edge cluster: the docs need synchronized time across the hosts, and each host keeps its own TUI or user-data setting"
               else empty end)
            else empty end ) ]
  reproduce:
  - 'for s in {{ (.entity.spec.cloudConfig.ntpServers // []) | join(" ") }}; do dig +short $s; nc -zu -w 2 $s 123 && echo "$s answers on udp/123"; done   # from this machine, not from the site'
  fix:
    owner: palette
    text: Warn in the validate route when a vSphere or a multi-node edge cluster names no NTP server.
  evidence:
  - kind: source
    note: Palette refuses an NTP server that is not an IPv4 address, an IPv6 address, or a DNS name
  - kind: doc
    ref: https://docs.spectrocloud.com/clusters/data-center/vmware/create-manage-vmware-clusters/
    note: we recommend specifying NTP servers; without them, time drift issues
  - kind: doc
    ref: https://docs.spectrocloud.com/clusters/edge/site-deployment/cluster-deployment/
    note: NTP servers correctly configured in a multi-node cluster; all nodes must have their time synchronized
  tests:
  - fault: fixtures/vsphere/ntp-empty.json
    clean: fixtures/vsphere/clean.json
  - fault: fixtures/edge/ntp-bad.json
    clean: fixtures/edge/clean.json
- id: vsphere-ip-pool-capacity
  title: The IP pool of the PCG has the addresses the cluster needs
  engines:
  - vsphere
  tier: palette
  severity: fail
  status: source
  when: (.entity.spec.cloudConfig.staticIp // false) and ((.account.metadata.annotations.overlordUid // "") != "")
  what: |
    Each node takes one address, a control plane pool reserves two more, and a worker pool one
    more, for the rolling update. Palette counts the range from `start` to `end` less the allotted
    addresses. It counts at the machine pool create, after the cluster document exists. The
    failure is `IPPoolExhausted`, and the cluster stays at `IpAllocationDone`. A pool restricted to a single
    cluster that another cluster holds is refused. `GET /v1/overlords/vsphere/{uid}/pools` lists
    the pools of the PCG; the check reads the pool of the first placement and sums the pools
    that use it.
  check:
    kind: palette
    method: GET
    path: /v1/overlords/vsphere/{{ .account.metadata.annotations.overlordUid }}/pools
    expr: |
      def ip2n: split(".") | map(tonumber) | reduce .[] as $o (0; . * 256 + $o);
      .account.metadata.annotations.overlordUid as $ol | (.entity.spec.cloudConfig.placement // {}) as $cp
      | ([ .entity.spec.machinepoolconfig[] | { pool: .poolConfig.name, size: (.poolConfig.size // 0), extra: (if (.poolConfig.isControlPlane // false) then 2 else 1 end),
            uid: ((((.cloudConfig.placements // []) | first) // $cp).network.parentPoolUid // $cp.network.parentPoolUid // "") } ]) as $pools
      | ([ $pools[] | .uid | select(. != "") ] | first) as $uid
      | if $uid == null then []
        elif (.response.ok | not) then ["Palette cannot list the IP pools of PCG \($ol): \(.response.body.code // .response.status): \(.response.body.message // "")"]
        else ([ (.response.body.items // [])[] | select(.metadata.uid == $uid) ] | first) as $ip
          | if $ip == null then ["no IP pool \($uid) on PCG \($ol): the placement names it as parentPoolUid"]
            else ([ $pools[] | select(.uid == $uid) ]) as $mine
              | ([ $mine[] | .size + .extra ] | add) as $need
              | (($ip.spec.pool.end | ip2n) - ($ip.spec.pool.start | ip2n) + 1) as $total
              | (($ip.status.allottedIps // []) | length) as $used
              | ($total - $used) as $free
              | [ ( if ($ip.spec.restrictToSingleCluster // false) and ($ip.status.inUse // false) then "IP pool \($ip.metadata.name // $uid) is restricted to a single cluster and in use by \(($ip.status.associatedClusters // []) | join(", ")): Palette refuses another cluster on it" else empty end ),
                  ( if $need > $free then "IP pool \($ip.metadata.name // $uid) has \($free) free of \($total) addresses (\($used) allotted), and the pools \([ $mine[] | .pool ] | join(", ")) need \($need): one for each node, plus 2 for a control plane pool and 1 for a worker pool; Palette answers IPPoolExhausted, and the cluster stays at IpAllocationDone" else empty end ) ]
            end
        end
  reproduce:
  - '{{ palette_curl }} "${PALETTE_API:-https://api.spectrocloud.com}/v1/overlords/vsphere/{{ .account.metadata.annotations.overlordUid }}/pools" | jq ''.items[] | {uid: .metadata.uid, name: .metadata.name, start: .spec.pool.start, end: .spec.pool.end, allotted: (.status.allottedIps | length), single: .spec.restrictToSingleCluster, inUse: .status.inUse}'''
  fix:
    owner: palette
    text: Count the free addresses of the pool in the validate route, as the machine pool create does.
  evidence:
  - kind: source
    note: free is the range less the allotted and the extra addresses; IPPoolExhausted
  - kind: source
    note: extra is 1, 2 for a control plane pool, 0 with RollingUpdateScaleIn
  - kind: doc
    ref: https://docs.spectrocloud.com/clusters/pcg/manage-pcg/create-manage-node-pool/
    note: two more IPs for a control plane pool and one for a worker pool; with too few, the cluster is not deployed
  tests:
  - fault: fixtures/vsphere/ip-pool-exhausted.json
    clean: fixtures/vsphere/clean.json
  - fault: fixtures/vsphere/ip-pool-single-cluster.json
- id: vsphere-static-ip-pool
  title: A static vSphere cluster names an IP pool on each placement
  engines:
  - vsphere
  tier: static
  severity: fail
  status: source
  what: |
    With `staticIp` on the cluster, each placement network of a pool needs `parentPoolUid`, the
    uid of an IP pool of the PCG; the converter refuses an empty one. With `staticIp` off, no
    placement network can set `staticIp`; the converter refuses the pair. The docs say an IPAM
    pool is required for static addresses. A pool with no placements takes the placement of the
    cluster. `vsphere-ip-pool-capacity` reads the pool itself.
  check:
    kind: static
    expr: |
      (.entity.spec.cloudConfig.staticIp // false) as $static | (.entity.spec.cloudConfig.placement // {}) as $cp
      | [ .entity.spec.machinepoolconfig[] | .poolConfig.name as $p | ((.cloudConfig.placements // []) | if length == 0 then [$cp] else . end)[] | (.network // $cp.network // {}) as $n
          | ( if $static and (($n.parentPoolUid // "") == "") then "pool \($p), network \($n.networkName // "?"): staticIp is on and parentPoolUid is empty; the converter refuses it (\"ParentPoolUid should not be empty\")" else empty end ),
            ( if ($static | not) and ($n.staticIp // false) then "pool \($p), network \($n.networkName // "?"): the cluster is DHCP (staticIp false) and the placement network sets staticIp true; the converter refuses the pair" else empty end ) ]
  fix:
    owner: none
    text: The check exists in the converter; strata-preflight runs it before the request.
  evidence:
  - kind: source
    note: Palette checks the static IP data of each placement when it converts the network config
  - kind: doc
    ref: https://docs.spectrocloud.com/clusters/data-center/vmware/create-manage-vmware-clusters/
    note: an IPAM pool is required to assign static IP addresses to the nodes
  tests:
  - fault: fixtures/vsphere/static-no-pool.json
    clean: fixtures/vsphere/clean.json
  - fault: fixtures/vsphere/dhcp-static-placement.json
    clean: fixtures/vsphere/dhcp-clean.json
